  «text (5140,897) 0.8 5 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Notes:\n* SIMCLK is NOT an actual device pin...\n* This device contains an internal oscillator.\n   However, that is not used for emulation.\n   Instead, SIMCLK is used to sychronize the\n   micro-controller to the QSpice simulation.\n   Each falling edge of SIMCLK steps the device\n   by 1 instruction cycle.  For this device,\n   one instruction cycle = 4 oscillator cycles.\n* Set OscFreq to match device oscillator \n   frequency as defined in the *.hex/*.elf\n   configuration bits."»
  «text (-3180,2272) 1.6 5 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿PIC16F1521x Test Fixture"»
  «text (-3000,-2691) 1 5 0 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿.param OscFreq=4Meg\n.param CyclesPerInst=4\n.param InstHz=OscFreq/CyclesPerInst"»
  «text (-3050,-2550) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Device Clock Parameters"»
  «text (3201,889) 1.25 14 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿"Charlieplexed" LEDs"»
  «text (1650,-2550) 1 7 0 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿.tran 5m"»
